  "description": "This walk visits the Fern Valley just north west of St Helier. The peaceful area includes a circular loop walk taking you through a large meadow and semi-mature deciduous woodland, with pretty streams and fern-covered c\u00f4tils.The area is alive with wildflowers, such as Bluebells and Primrose, which attract varied butterfly species, while Red Squirrels, voles, and birds of prey like Kestrels are common sights. This secluded landscape, featuring oak and ash trees, is an ideal spot for a leisurely picnic, often accompanied by sightings of Great Spotted Woodpeckers and dragonflies.You can continue your walking in the nearbyWaterworks Valley.",
